<%# The native time control plus a clear button of our own, because no engine ships
    one: iOS Safari's wheel picker has no empty position to scroll back to, and the
    desktop engines only clear on a Delete keypress inside a focused segment. An event
    whose start time is genuinely unknown has to be enterable somewhere.

    The control stays native — a text field beside a native date draws its underline at
    a different height on mobile Safari (see the input[type="time"] skin in
    application.css). The caller keeps its own <label>; this is the field itself. %>
<%# locals: (name:, value:) %>
<div class="time-field" data-controller="time-field">
  <%= time_field_tag name, value,
        data: { time_field_target: "input",
                action: "input->time-field#refresh change->time-field#refresh" } %>
  <button type="button" class="time-field__clear icon-button" hidden
          data-time-field-target="clear" data-action="time-field#clear"
          aria-label="<%= t('shared.time_field.clear') %>">
    <span class="ph ph-x" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </button>
</div>
